# Database, RLS and RPC controls

- Database/Canonical or Shared Database Control must authorize database packets and own applicable migration/RLS/RPC paths.
- Use one ordered migration history and one writer per packet.
- No remote Supabase mutation without an explicit environment gate.
- Local changes must be rebuildable from zero with deterministic synthetic seed data.
- Enable and test RLS for exposed tenant-sensitive tables; prohibit unconditional tenant read policies.
- Centralize reviewed JWT/claim helpers instead of duplicating expressions.
- Require own-tenant positive and cross-tenant/unauthorized negative tests.
- Restricted RPCs must validate tenant/actor context, least privilege, errors and audit behavior.
- Project B must not redefine Canonical truth or KDB-owned schema semantics.